node_modules/
dist/
.refs/
#
# `assets/` is committed, apart from the two trees that cannot be. Everything
# under it is derivative of the GPLv2/CC inputs ASSETS.md records and carries
# their terms; the attribution lives there.
#
# `ml/` is 36 GB -- 28 GB of third-party model weights whose shards are each
# well past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, a 2.7 GB pip cache, and a venv full of
# absolute Windows paths that would be broken for anyone else anyway.
#
# `download/` is the 425 MB upstream archive. `fetch-assets.mjs` re-fetches it
# and checks it against a recorded SHA-256, and `extracted/` already holds every
# file the port consumes, so committing it would buy nothing and would have cost
# a Git LFS dependency for the whole repository.
#
assets/ml/
assets/download/
oracle/build/
*.log
.vite/
coverage/

# JetBrains
.idea/

oracle/build/

# Python bytecode from the material pipeline tools
__pycache__/
*.pyc
